    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22480" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-concessus</span></b> , a, um,
		adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>not allowed</i>, <i>impossible</i> (not
			ante-Aug. and rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hymenaei,</span>”
				<i>unlawful</i>, <i>forbidden</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 1, 651</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ignes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 10, 153</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 9, 638</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum totum exprimere paene sit homini
					inconcessum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 10, 2, 26</span></i>
			.</div>
